.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_PKEY-ML-DSA 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_PKEY-ML-DSA ,
.Nm EVP_KEYMGMT-ML-DSA ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY-ML-DSA-44 ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY-ML-DSA-65 ,
.Nm EVP_PKEY-ML-DSA-87
.Nd EVP_PKEY ML-DSA keytype and algorithm support
.Sh DESCRIPTION
ML-DSA implements the algorithms
.Sy ML-DSA-44 ,
.Sy ML-DSA-65
and
.Sy ML-DSA-87 .
The key types
.Sy EVP_PKEY_ML_DSA_44 ,
.Sy EVP_PKEY_ML_DSA_65
and
.Sy EVP_PKEY_ML_DSA_87
are implemented in OpenSSL's default and FIPS providers.
These implementations support the associated key, containing the public
key
.Em pub
and the private key
.Em priv .
.Pp
Each of the different key types has an associated security category.
This value is one of 2, 3 or 5 for key types
.Sy ML-DSA-44 ,
.Sy ML-DSA-65
and
.Sy ML-DSA-87
respectively, which correspond to security strengths of 128, 192 and 256
repsectively.
.Ss Keygen Parameters
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqseed" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_ML_DSA_SEED Ns ) <octet string>
The seed can be used to generate the private and public key components
in a deterministic manner.
The length of the value supplied must be 32 bytes.
When this value is not supplied the seed is generated randomly using a
DRBG.
.Pp
Generated keys default to retaining the seed used.
The seed is also by default retained when keys are loaded from
.Sy PKCS#8
files in the seed format.
When available, the seed parameter is also used during key export and
import, with keys (by default) regenerated from the seed even when also
provided on import.
See
.Sx Provider configuration parameters
below for related controls.
.Pp
When the seed is retained, it is also available as a
.Sy gettable
parameter, and private key output to
.Sy PKCS#8
files will by default include the seed.
When the seed was not initially known, or was not retained,
.Sy PKCS#8
private key files will contain only the private key in FIPS 204
.Qo Li sk Qc
format.
.It \(dqproperties" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_PROPERTIES Ns ) <UTF8 string>
Sets properties to be used when fetching algorithm implementations used
for ML-DSA hashing operations.
.El
.Pp
Use
.Xr EVP_PKEY_CTX_set_params 3
after calling
.Xr EVP_PKEY_keygen_init 3 .
.Ss Common ML-DSA parameters
In addition to the common parameters that all keytypes should support
(see
.Xr provider-keymgmt 7 ,
the implementation of these key types support the parameters listed
below.
These are gettable using
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get_octet_string_param 3
or
.Xr EVP_PKEY_get_params 3 .
They can be initialised via
.Xr EVP_PKEY_fromdata 3 ,
and are returned by
.Xr EVP_PKEY_todata 3
given a suitable
.Em selection .
Once a public or private key is configured, it can no longer be
modified, nor can another key component be added.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqpub" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_PUB_KEY Ns ) <octet string>
The encoded public key value of size 1312, 1952 or 2592 bytes depending
on the respective key type of
.Sy ML-DSA-44 ,
.Sy ML-DSA-65
or
.Sy ML-DSA-87 .
.It \(dqpriv" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_PRIV_KEY Ns ) <octet string>
The encoded private key value of size 2560, 4032 or 4896 bytes depending
on the respective key type of
.Sy ML-DSA-44 ,
.Sy ML-DSA-65
or
.Sy ML-DSA-87 .
.El
.Ss Provider configuration parameters
See the description of the
.Sy -provparam
option in
.Xr openssl 1
to learn how to set provider configuration parameters in the command
line tools.
See
.Xr OSSL_PROVIDER_add_conf_parameter 3
to learn how to set provider configuration options programmatically.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Qo Li ml-dsa.retain_seed Qc No ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_ML_DSA_RETAIN_SEED Ns ) <UTF8 string>
When set to a string representing a false boolean value (see
.Xr OSSL_PROVIDER_conf_get_bool 3 Ns ),
the seed will not be retained after key generation or key import from a
seed value.
If the resulting key is then written to a PKCS#8 object, it will contain
only the FIPS 204
.Qo Li sk Qc
key.
.It Qo Li ml-dsa.prefer_seed Qc No ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_ML_DSA_PREFER_SEED Ns ) <UTF8 string>
When decoding PKCS#8 objects that contain both a seed and the FIPS 204
.Qo Li sk Qc
private key, the seed is by default used to regenerate the key, and the
companion private key is ignored.
When this configuration parameter is set to a string representing a
false boolean value (see
.Xr OSSL_PROVIDER_conf_get_bool 3 Ns ),
the seed is ignored (neither used to regenerate the key, nor retained),
and the companion key is used instead.
.It Qo Li ml-dsa.input_formats Qc No ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_ML_DSA_INPUT_FORMATS Ns ) <UTF8 string>
List of enabled private key input formats when parsing PKCS#8 objects.
List elements are separated by commas, spaces or tabs.
The list of enabled formats can be specified in the configuration file,
as seen in the
.Sx EXAMPLES
section below, or the via the
.Sy -provparam
command-line option (see also
.Xr OSSL_PROVIDER_add_conf_parameter 3 Ns ).
.Pp
Values specified on the command-line override any configuration file
settings.
By default all the supported formats are enabled.
The supported formats are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Qo Li seed-priv Qc :
This format represents
.Sy PKCS#8
objects in which both the FIPS 204 32-byte
.Sy ξ
seed and the secret key
.Sy sk
are present in the private key as part of the DER encoding of the ASN.1
sequence:
.Bd -literal
    ML-DSA-PrivateKey ::= CHOICE {
      seed [0] IMPLICIT OCTET STRING (SIZE (32)),
      expandedKey OCTET STRING (SIZE (2560 | 4032 | 4896)),
      both SEQUENCE {
        seed OCTET STRING (SIZE (32)),
        expandedKey OCTET STRING (SIZE (2560 | 4032 | 4896)) } }
.Ed
.Pp
If the
.Qo Li seed-priv Qc
format is not included in the list, this format will not be recognised
on input.
.It Qo Li seed-only Qc :
This format represents
.Sy PKCS#8
objects in which only the 32-byte FIPS 204
.Sy ξ
seed is present in the above sequence.
If the
.Qo Li seed-only Qc
format is not included in the list, this format will not be recognised
on input.
.It Qo Li priv-only Qc :
This format represents
.Sy PKCS#8
objects in which only the FIPS 204 private key
.Sy sk
is present in the above sequence.
If the
.Qo Li priv-only Qc
format is not included in the list, this format will not be recognised
on input.
.It Qo Li oqskeypair Qc :
This format represents
.Sy PKCS#8
objects in which the private key is a DER encoding of an octet string
containing the concatenaton of the FIPS 204 private key
.Sy sk
and the public key
.Sy pk .
This encoding is used in some builds of the
.Qo Li oqsprovider Qc .
If the
.Qo Li oqskeypair Qc
format is not included in the list, this format will not be recognised
on input.
.It Qo Li bare-seed Qc :
This format represents
.Sy PKCS#8
objects in which the private key contains the 32-byte FIPS 204 seed
.Sy ξ
without any ASN.1 encapsulation.
If the
.Qo Li bare-seed Qc
format is not included in the list, this format will not be recognised
on input.
.It Qo Li bare-priv Qc :
This format represents
.Sy PKCS#8
objects in which the private key contains the FIPS 204 secret key
.Sy sk
without any ASN.1 encapsulation.
If the
.Qo Li bare-priv Qc
format is not included in the list, this format will not be recognised
on input.
.El
.It Qo Li ml-dsa.output_formats Qc No ( Ns Sy OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_ML_DSA_OUTPUT_FORMATS Ns ) <UTF8 string>
Ordered list of enabled private key output formats when writing
.Sy PKCS#8
files.
List elements are separated by commas, spaces or tabs.
The list of enabled formats can be specified in the configuration file,
as seen in the
.Sx EXAMPLES
section below, or the via the
.Sy -provparam
command-line option.
.Pp
This supports the same set of formats as described under
.Qo Li ml-dsa.input_formats Qc
above.
The order in which elements are listed is important, the selected format
will be the first one that is possible to output.
If the key seed is known, the first listed format will be selected.
If the key seed is not known, the first format that omits the seed will
be selected.
The default order is equivalent to
.Qo Li seed-priv Qc
first and
.Qo Li priv-only Qc
second, with both seed and key output when the seed is available, and
just the key otherwise.
If
.Qo Li seed-only Qc
is listed first, then the seed will be output without the key when
available, otherwise the output will have just the key.
If
.Qo Li priv-only Qc
is listed first, then just the key is output regardless of whether the
seed is present.
The legacy
.Qo Li oqskeypair Qc ,
.Qo Li bare-seed Qc
and
.Qo Li bare-priv Qc
formats can also be output, by listing those first.
.El
.Sh CONFORMING TO
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It FIPS 204
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
An
.Sy EVP_PKEY
context can be obtained by calling:
.Bd -literal
    EVP_PKEY_CTX *pctx =
        EVP_PKEY_CTX_new_from_name(NULL, "ML-DSA-44", NULL);
.Ed
.Pp
An
.Sy ML-DSA-44
key can be generated like this:
.Bd -literal
    pkey = EVP_PKEY_Q_keygen(NULL, NULL, "ML-DSA-44");
.Ed
.Pp
The key pair components can be extracted from a key by calling:
.Bd -literal
    /* Sizes large enough for ML-DSA-87 */
    uint8_t pub[2592], priv[4896], seed[32]:
    size_t priv_len, pub_len, seed_len;

    EVP_PKEY_get_octet_string_param(pkey, OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_ML_DSA_SEED,
                                    seed, sizeof(seed), &seed_len);
    EVP_PKEY_get_octet_string_param(pkey, OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_PRIV_KEY,
                                    priv, sizeof(priv), &priv_len);
    EVP_PKEY_get_octet_string_param(pkey, OSSL_PKEY_PARAM_PUB_KEY,
                                    pub, sizeof(pub), &pub_len));
.Ed
.Pp
An
.Sy ML-DSA
private key in seed format can be converted to a key in the FIPS 204
.Sy sk
format by running:
.Bd -literal
    $ openssl pkey -provparam ml-dsa.retain_seed=no \e
        -in seed-only.pem -out priv-only.pem
.Ed
.Pp
To generate an, e.g.,
.Sy ML-DSA-65
key, in FIPS 204
.Sy sk
format, you can run:
.Bd -literal
    $ openssl genpkey -provparam ml-dsa.retain_seed=no \e
        -algorithm ml-dsa-65 -out priv-only.pem
.Ed
.Pp
If you have a
.Sy PKCS#8
file with both a seed and a key, and prefer to import the companion key
rather than the seed, you can run:
.Bd -literal
    $ openssl pkey -provparam ml-dsa.prefer_seed=no \e
        -in seed-priv.pem -out priv-only.pem
.Ed
.Pp
In the
.Sy openssl.cnf
file, this looks like:
.Bd -literal
    openssl_conf = openssl_init

    [openssl_init]
    providers = providers_sect

    # Can be referenced in one or more provider sections
    [ml_dsa_sect]
    prefer_seed = yes
    retain_seed = yes
    # OQS legacy formats disabled
    input_formats = seed-priv, seed-only, priv-only
    # Output either the seed alone, or else the key alone
    output_formats = seed-only, priv-only

    [providers_sect]
    default = default_sect
    # Or perhaps just: base = default_sect
    base = base_sect

    [default_sect]
    ml-dsa = ml_dsa_sect

    [base_sect]
    ml-dsa = ml_dsa_sect
.Ed
